    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42056" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rūsellae</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rōsell-</span></b> ), ārum,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Etruria</i>, now <i>Rosello.</i>—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rūsel-lānus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rōsell-</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Rusellœ</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					10, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">37</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colonia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 8, § 51</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rūsel-lāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Rusellœ</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 28, 45
					<i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
